    "narrative": "Woke from a dream set in the workshop my late mentor kept behind the house, where I learned to sand a chair leg without rushing. In the dream he said nothing and just handed me the next piece. Two years since the funeral and I still save up things to tell him. I started these morning pages because he said hands and words both need a daily practice. Maybe writing is how I keep the lesson going."
